<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3237" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμ-άζω</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be in full
				bloom, at the prime</i>: </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> of persons, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.134
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				335e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. σώματι, ῥώμῃ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				4.4.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				310d
			</span></i>, etc.; of cities and states, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.57
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.28
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὸ σῶμα ἀπὸ τῶν λ́ ἐτῶν μέχρι
					τῶν έ καὶ λ́</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1390b9
				</span></i>
			; 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ τῶν νέων πράττειν</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				122
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>flourish, abound in</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλούτῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.29
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρασκευῇ πάσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεότητι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.20
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναυσὶκαὶ χρήμασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					3.163
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c.
			inf., <i>to be strong enough</i> to do, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				3.1.25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of things,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ὁ πυρετός, ἡ νόσος</span>
			<i>is at its height</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				2.29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epid.</u>
				1.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.49
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ πάθους ἀκμάζοντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Lib.</u>
					p.31
				</span></i>
			 O.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ὁ πόλεμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.3
				</span></i>
			; of corn, <i>to be ripe</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡνίκα . . ἀκμάζοι [ὁ θυμός</span>]
			when passion <i>is at its height</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				70d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμάζουσα ῥώμη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					4.3.3
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμάζει πάντα ἐπιμελείας
			δεόμενα</span> require <i>the utmost</i> care, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				4.2.40
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> impers., c.
				inf., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμάζει βρετέων
				ἔχεσθαι</span> '<i>tis time</i> to . ., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				97
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῦν γὰρ ἀ. Πειθὼ . .
				ξυγκαταβῆναι</span> now '<i>tis time</i> for her to . .,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				726
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
